WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Let's talk about one money habit that protects everything else: an emergency fund.

00:08.000 --> 00:20.000
An emergency fund is money you set aside for one job: urgent costs you couldn't plan for.

00:20.000 --> 00:34.000
Think of a car repair you need to get to work, a surprise medical bill, a laptop that dies before finals, or a trip home when family needs you.

00:34.000 --> 00:48.000
It's not for things you can plan for, like textbooks, rent, or a spring break trip. Those belong in your regular budget.

00:48.000 --> 01:02.000
Why does it matter? Without a cushion, a surprise often goes on a credit card, where interest can make it cost more for months.

01:02.000 --> 01:16.000
With a cushion, a bad surprise stays a bad day instead of turning into a bad year.

01:16.000 --> 01:30.000
And if you do use it, that's exactly what it's for. Use it, then rebuild it a little at a time.

01:30.000 --> 01:40.000
Next up: how much you need.
